{"name":"Dance Studio","hex":"#064d83","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dance studio","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A studio where dancing skills can be practiced and trained."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance_studio"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dance studio","blocks":[{"text":"A dance studio is a space in which dancers learn or rehearse. The term typically refers to the specific room used for dancing, but it may also be used for any particular establishment or building as a whole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Dancing_lesson_16507650.jpg/330px-Dancing_lesson_16507650.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_studio","wikidata":"Q1561361"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance","wikidata":"Q11639"},{"title":"Studio","blocks":[{"text":"A studio is a space set aside for creative work of any kind, including art, dance, music and theater."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Bashkirtseff_-_In_the_Studio.jpg/330px-Bashkirtseff_-_In_the_Studio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Studio","wikidata":"Q746628"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/